1
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for a certain day
drifting on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:24,660
when I kick a pebble, even my shoes fly off.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,920
onto the head of the
carpenter I was choking,

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I'm still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I try to send you some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
Katsushika's sky, one yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,140
The streetscape is strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed-hat water bottle,

9
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,460
the sunset falls toward the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end just like this, won't it?

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,020
Shibamata again, even happiness is lost.

12
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:24,660
Because I'm a fool who only
realized after listening.

13
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:53,160
Whatever, senpai, Ryo-san!

14
00:01:53,340 --> 00:01:56,400
Ryo-chan, I'll be sure to pass
that on to the Chief for you.

15
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:58,300
Hey, what do you think you're doing!

16
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:00,700
See!

17
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,340
Ryo-san's grandfather is,

18
00:02:07,390 --> 00:02:09,820
I think he's supposed to be over 100 years old,
a real long-liver.

19
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:10,480
Well.

20
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:15,060
106 years old!?

21
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:18,500
At that age, he still lives alone?

22
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:26,040
No matter what the old folks say,
he just won't budge from Tsukudajima.

23
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:28,800
He's the very picture of a stubborn old geezer,
honestly.

24
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:32,460
He must be really attached to Tsukudajima.

25
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:34,820
Yeah, well.

26
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:41,520
That area is one of the few old Edo-style towns still left,
you know.

27
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:51,360
Come on!

28
00:02:52,460 --> 00:02:54,690
Tsukudajima was originally

29
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:59,300
a fishing village that Tokugawa Ieyasu
developed as part of the Edo development project.

30
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:06,500
I hear that shirauo fishing, supplied to the shogunate,
was the pride of the Tsukudajima fishermen.

31
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:11,320
So was your grandfather a
fisherman originally, senpai?

32
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:12,202
No,

33
00:03:12,252 --> 00:03:17,080
my grandpa bought the small fish caught
in nets and ran a tsukudani business.

34
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:21,140
So your father in Asakusa took over that shop,
didn't he?

35
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:21,900
Well,

36
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:30,980
it's been a while since I last came here,

37
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:34,280
and Tsukudajima has changed quite a lot.

38
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:39,780
It's certainly a little
different from what I imagined.

39
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:42,820
I think Grandpa's place was around here.

40
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:53,320
I don't see a nameplate
that says Ryotsu anywhere

41
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:54,000
Yeah.

42
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:56,240
If it's a Kamechu, I'll trade you.

43
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:58,240
I don't have a Kamechu.

44
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:00,240
But where do you suppose Kamechu is?

45
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:01,920
Nobody has one, though.

46
00:04:02,260 --> 00:04:05,120
There's that cave next to Higurashi
Village you can't get into, right?

47
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:07,500
If you use Flash there to get in,
there's one inside.

48
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:09,940
Really, Officer?

49
00:04:10,356 --> 00:04:14,380
By the way, do you guys know where the house
of an old man named Ryotsu is around here?

50
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:19,420
Senpai, watch out!

51
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:23,300
Are you all right, senpai?

52
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:27,720
What's this?
Isn't it a radio-controlled toy?

53
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:29,460
Who the heck is that?

54
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:34,220
Sorry, sorry.

55
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,320
G-Gramps!

56
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,520
Grandpa.

57
00:04:44,520 --> 00:05:12,740
Uoooooooooooooh!

58
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:15,880
Wasn't it a high score after all?!

59
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:18,140
Kitoku? Who did?

60
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:21,640
This morning Dad got word
that Grandpa got a kitoku!

61
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:25,645
I stayed up all night playing games, and

62
00:05:25,695 --> 00:05:27,560
I got an amazing score!

63
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:31,340
I told everyone! Kitoku! Kitoku!

64
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:34,232
A record-breaking score,

65
00:05:34,282 --> 00:05:37,800
abbreviated, ki, to, ku...

66
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:40,800
Ugh! Don't come up with such
a serious-sounding abbreviation!

67
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:44,020
Looks like there's no need to visit,
so I'm heading home.

68
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:45,700
Let's go, Nakagawa.

69
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:48,960
Going home already? You just got here!

70
00:05:48,960 --> 00:06:03,920
Will any visitor ever come to see an old wreck like this again?
Will they come, won't they, will they come, won't they...

71
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:05,160
That old geezer.

72
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:08,380
Senpai, why don't you stay a little longer?

73
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:11,380
I'll make up some excuse
to the Chief for you.

74
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:14,540
I bet he really wanted
someone to come visit him.

75
00:06:21,860 --> 00:06:30,360
Since you came all this way,
why not have lunch with me?

76
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,320
Lunch?

77
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,640
Would you consider it?

78
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:34,460
No, I think we'll head home after all.

79
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:37,700
It hurts.

80
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:40,320
If the deadly illness comes back...

81
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:41,580
Are you all right?

82
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:43,940
The crossroads right in front of -

83
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:46,460
It's fine, my eyes are going blurry.

84
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:48,120
My body feels far away.

85
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,880
My mind feels far away too.

86
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:52,760
Have mercy on the poor thing.

87
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:54,720
a life of just 106 years.

88
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:57,460
dying alone and lonely.

89
00:06:57,460 --> 00:07:00,720
tomorrow's top headline
for the commissioner.

90
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:05,560
Well, you there,
looks like you're going to find that prince.

91
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:07,980
Oh my, aren't you ashamed
of yourself as a human being?

92
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:08,700
As a human being.

93
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:09,960
Really, right?

94
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:10,040
Yes.

95
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,700
Alright, alright.

96
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:13,960
There's a shop I want to go to.

97
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,180
H-here?

98
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:24,760
Look, it's even in the info magazine!

99
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:27,640
A shop like this that's popular with the gals,
you know.

100
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:38,080
I see.

101
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:47,380
Hey, if you gobble it down that fast,

102
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:48,700
you'll choke on it.

103
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:51,440
This korata

104
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:53,300
is really delicious!

105
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:55,260
So is it called korata?

106
00:07:55,260 --> 00:07:57,840
Roast lamb rata, that's the proper name.

107
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,560
Shortened, it's just "this rata."

108
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,400
Since you're treating us to it,

109
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,880
Nao-sharanmai!

110
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:04,180
I'm Kankichi.

111
00:08:04,180 --> 00:08:07,260
That's right, that's right.

112
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:09,840
Kankichi, my son these days.

113
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:11,900
My father is Ginji.

114
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:14,360
Yeah, yeah, Ginji, Ginji.

115
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:17,240
Ginji, who runs a ramen shop in Aoyama,

116
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:19,380
and runs a tsukudani shop in Asakusa.

117
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:20,280
Enough already!

118
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,300
I'm not feeding you anymore.

119
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,420
Give it here, I'll eat it!

120
00:08:25,260 --> 00:08:26,046
Well, you see,

121
00:08:26,096 --> 00:08:29,440
I've got 24 grandchildren, so forgive me.

122
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:32,720
Cheat sheet, gyapa-mi.

123
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:33,280
What?

124
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:40,400
Gal's panties are about to show.
Shortened to...

125
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:42,940
Don't shorten it! Just hurry up and eat!

126
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:52,040
Tsukudajima has changed quite a lot,
hasn't it.

127
00:08:52,580 --> 00:08:54,682
New buildings keep going
up one after another,

128
00:08:54,732 --> 00:08:56,720
and there's no charm left at all.

129
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:01,300
Come to think of it,
when I was a kid, let alone skyscrapers,

130
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:04,800
there wasn't even Tsukishima.

131
00:09:10,560 --> 00:09:12,760
W-when exactly was that?

132
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:18,220
Must be nearly a hundred years ago now.

133
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:21,940
That's off by an order of magnitude.

134
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:22,960
This one's...

135
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:25,180
Back then, that...

136
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:26,940
there wasn't even the Tsukuda Ohashi.

137
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:28,240
Mm.

138
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,060
There used to be a ferry, you know.

139
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:31,160
I've heard of it.

140
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:34,080
From Akaishi-chō on the
opposite bank to Tsukuda,

141
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:36,040
it was only a four or five minute trip.

142
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:38,120
It was close for going to Ginza, too,

143
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:40,260
and since it was free,
we used it all the time.

144
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,720
You rode it as a baby too, you know.

145
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:44,640
Really?

146
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:46,400
I don't really remember.

147
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:51,180
That was back when I still
ran the tsukudani shop.

148
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:55,300
Your mom came to pick up
ingredients for the tsukudani.

149
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:59,280
I ended up taking you along to Asakusa.

150
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:03,560
On the boat, I dropped you into the river.

151
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:06,840
Dropped me? Then what happened?

152
00:10:07,140 --> 00:10:09,660
The boat set off as if nothing had happened.

153
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:10,140
What?

154
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:12,406
Right in the middle of the river,

155
00:10:12,456 --> 00:10:16,480
a ferry crew member spotted
you floating in the Sumida River.

156
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:19,520
This baby's drowning!

157
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:26,820
It's a fond memory now.

158
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:30,020
You nearly drowned him,
and now you want to make it a fond memory!

159
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:33,060
Gyapa-mi again. Hahaha, there we go.

160
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:34,100
Kankichi!

161
00:10:34,660 --> 00:10:40,940
Was it around here?

162
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:42,420
Whoa!

163
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:43,220
What's wrong?

164
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:46,940
My house is gone!

165
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:52,900
In the few hours I looked away,
it got snapped up by developers.

166
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:53,840
What? No way.

167
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:55,940
Just kidding!

168
00:10:55,940 --> 00:10:59,600
My house is over there.

169
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:03,960
That high-rise condo?

170
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:06,340
Where did they even get that kind of money?

171
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:13,480
All the neighbors left together too,
and we got plenty of relocation money.

172
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:16,720
I love high places, you know.

173
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:23,480
Hopeless.
He has no attachment to anything at all.

174
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:33,780
Wow, what a view.

175
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:35,680
You can see Yurakucho Marion from here.

176
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:39,480
On clear days,
you can even see Tsutenkaku in Osaka.

177
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:40,540
Really?

178
00:11:40,540 --> 00:11:42,060
Just kidding!

179
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:43,160
There's no way you can see that.

180
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:43,440
Here goes!

181
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:46,500
Nyahahahaha!

182
00:11:46,620 --> 00:11:49,194
Hey! If you're living this luxuriously,

183
00:11:49,244 --> 00:11:51,040
why are you begging people for lunch!

184
00:11:52,060 --> 00:11:54,820
Kanbē, I'm borrowing some garam masala.

185
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:55,540
Yeah.

186
00:11:58,100 --> 00:11:59,240
Who's that?

187
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:01,940
Something about Gara,
Garabara earning money.

188
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:05,320
Heh heh, the neighbor really likes cooking.

189
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:09,810
I'll make you some
authentic Indian curry later,

190
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:10,660
Kanbē.

191
00:12:10,660 --> 00:12:12,720
I'm looking forward to that.

192
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,200
Moto-san.

193
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:21,867
Lend me your lacrosse racket, will ya?

194
00:12:21,917 --> 00:12:23,520
Mine's broken.

195
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:27,460
Go ahead and grab one, Motojiro.

196
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:30,420
That old geezer playing lacrosse?

197
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:38,100
Kan-san isn't going home, you know.

198
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:46,520
Thanks for your trouble. Just leave it out for me to eat later.
We've never locked the front door, not since the old days.

199
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:54,760
Besides, an old man living alone who forgets where he put things is careless.
This place is just like a tenement, so it's fine.

200
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:59,100
You think there's anything
worth stealing here?

201
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:04,600
That's not what I'm saying!
What if a burglar broke in?

202
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:32,620
I've recently started an internet provider business,
you know.

203
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:35,600
Normal people don't start up internet providers,
you know.

204
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:37,920
Why don't you sign up?

205
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:40,640
How about a flat rate of 2,000 yen?

206
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:43,820
Honestly, how far will this high-tech,
trendy old geezer go?

207
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:53,540
I've never seen this game before.

208
00:13:53,540 --> 00:13:54,751
Well, of course you haven't.

209
00:13:54,801 --> 00:13:58,900
This is a brand-new game I made myself,
fresh off the press!

210
00:13:58,900 --> 00:14:01,940
What? You're making video games now too,
Grandpa?

211
00:14:02,380 --> 00:14:05,980
Alright, as a game critic,
I'll give it a try and test it out for you.

212
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:07,840
If you're going to play,
it's 1,000 yen a go.

213
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:18,600
No good.

214
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:24,760
I guess I'll throw in beer
and some snacks for free.

215
00:14:29,820 --> 00:14:30,620
Grill net.

216
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:31,060
Worth it.

217
00:14:38,540 --> 00:14:40,460
This is pretty well made, isn't it?

218
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:42,160
The bug fixing is done too.

219
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:44,180
All that's left is to put it on sale.

220
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:48,160
Something smells.

221
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:50,920
I see.

222
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:03,580
You made us waste our time.

223
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:11,580
Hey, Kanta, Kanta, Kanta, Kanta!

224
00:15:13,860 --> 00:15:15,820
I'm touched.

225
00:15:15,820 --> 00:15:17,740
So you finally noticed?

226
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:18,600
What the heck is this?

227
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:21,180
I was tied up by the burglar earlier.

228
00:15:21,740 --> 00:15:23,320
For short, it's "tea ceremony play."

229
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:25,440
Is this any time to be playing
around with abbreviations?

230
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:27,700
You didn't get hurt, did you, Grandpa?

231
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:29,300
I'm fine.

232
00:15:30,260 --> 00:15:32,280
More importantly, my precious...

233
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:36,640
My safe, which is more precious than my life,
has been stolen!

234
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:38,460
Damn it, what a disaster!

235
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:41,420
Was it me?

236
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:42,940
Your eyes...

237
00:15:45,140 --> 00:15:48,020
They tied up the gas valve.
It won't budge at all.

238
00:15:48,460 --> 00:15:50,440
Ugh, they've tied it up so thoroughly.

239
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:51,100
That's why.

240
00:15:51,140 --> 00:15:53,880
Fire! Somebody, come help!

241
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:58,120
Hey, it's useless.
This condo is fully soundproofed.

242
00:15:58,580 --> 00:16:00,400
No choice. We're going like this.

243
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:01,540
Yes, understood.

244
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:03,280
Wow, wow.

245
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:07,900
Make sure you shut off the gas.

246
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,420
Roger, roger.

247
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:14,860
What were you thinking,
cranking it up to full blast, you idiot?

248
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:16,640
Ow ow

249
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:18,100
Damn it.

250
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:25,200
It's no good, I can't put it out at all.

251
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:27,760
It'll spread on the wind!
Where's the fire extinguisher?

252
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:29,060
There's no such thing, no way.

253
00:16:29,060 --> 00:16:31,380
Buy a fire extinguisher before you buy a PC.

254
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:34,720
Come on!

255
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:42,940
Cockroach!

256
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:50,680
I thought I was going to die.

257
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:51,800
Make it easy on yourself.

258
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:52,840
Shut up!

259
00:16:53,640 --> 00:16:54,740
Hurry up, Kanpei!

260
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:01,440
Just hang in there.

261
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:04,080
The grill's sizzling,
spraying lots of water!

262
00:17:04,220 --> 00:17:04,620
Sizzle!

263
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:06,160
Sizzle! Look!

264
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,560
Hang in there! Hang in there!

265
00:17:09,940 --> 00:17:12,200
You're using me as a firefighter!

266
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:17,780
There he is!

267
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:20,400
I want to catch that culprit!

268
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:22,060
Right! After him!

269
00:17:23,020 --> 00:17:25,180
Wait! This way is faster!

270
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:28,460
These days,
condos sure are thoughtful, aren't they!

271
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:28,940
What?

272
00:17:29,940 --> 00:17:31,840
Skydiving!

273
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:43,480
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

274
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:45,040
Quicker than I expected You kicked me out!

275
00:17:45,340 --> 00:17:46,140
Are you trying to kill me!

276
00:17:46,980 --> 00:17:50,620
Over there,
the burglar ran off toward Sumiyoshi Shrine!

277
00:17:50,620 --> 00:17:53,540
Damn it, I'm definitely going to catch him!

278
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:54,780
Idiot!

279
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:56,380
There's a shortcut.

280
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:01,260
Isn't it awfully narrow?

281
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:05,320
One person would be fine, but with two
of us it'll surely be hard to get through.

282
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:07,820
Ugh!

283
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:12,940
What is it? Did something happen?

284
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,400
I went all out.

285
00:18:15,180 --> 00:18:17,520
Forget sideways, we'll go straight ahead.

286
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:18,240
I see.

287
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:20,540
There he is!

288
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:28,920
That hurts, Kazuo!

289
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:29,600
Shut up!

290
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:35,580
Wait! Give back my safe!

291
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:38,020
Who's dumb enough to stop
when someone says "Wait"?

292
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:40,580
What's he doing?

293
00:18:40,640 --> 00:18:41,580
Huh?

294
00:18:42,180 --> 00:18:43,600
Huh?

295
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:44,680
Huh?

296
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:49,040
That's it, I'm done!

297
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:50,560
I'm not chasing that thief anymore!

298
00:18:50,780 --> 00:18:52,020
I don't know anything about a safe!

299
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:54,120
What a thing to say, Kanta.

300
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:55,820
That safe holds

301
00:18:55,860 --> 00:18:59,300
all the keepsakes I
shared with your grandma.

302
00:18:59,820 --> 00:19:02,480
Without it, I can't go on living.

303
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:08,875
For this old man to be this fixated,

304
00:19:08,925 --> 00:19:10,920
those memories must be really precious

305
00:19:15,160 --> 00:19:17,678
Fine,

306
00:19:17,728 --> 00:19:21,260
all right, all right.

307
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:24,000
We just have to catch him, right?
Just catch him.

308
00:19:24,260 --> 00:19:25,560
Kanpei.

309
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:45,580
Thank goodness. Untie this rope for me.

310
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:47,760
What happened, Kan-san?

311
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:49,860
A burglar got me.

312
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:52,580
Well, that's a terrible misfortune.

313
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:57,540
By the way, that racket I
borrowed is working really well.

314
00:19:57,540 --> 00:20:00,980
I'm glad to hear that.

315
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:04,280
Hurry up,
or we'll lose sight of the burglar!

316
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:06,680
No need.

317
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:17,540
Go! Hindenburg Go!

318
00:20:17,940 --> 00:20:20,300
You even had something like this?!

319
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:24,473
To escape from Tsukudajima, he has to
cross Aioi Bridge, Katsutoki Bridge,

320
00:20:24,523 --> 00:20:25,434
Tsukida Bridge,

321
00:20:25,484 --> 00:20:28,560
or Chuo Bridge.

322
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:31,800
He's somewhere on the road
leading to one of those bridges!

323
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:33,300
We'll catch him!

324
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:39,920
Eeeeeeeh!

325
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:42,980
Haah!

326
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:44,380
Haah!

327
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:45,120
Haah!

328
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:45,900
Haah!

329
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:56,540
Don't underestimate my technique!

330
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:57,540
Don't underestimate my technique!

331
00:20:57,540 --> 00:20:59,900
Don't underestimate my technique!

332
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:01,880
Ugh!

333
00:21:12,580 --> 00:21:13,680
Wait a minute!

334
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:20,100
Hey, Kan-tarō, are you all right?

335
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:23,820
How many times do you
plan to kill your grandson?

336
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:25,160
It's closing, it's closing!

337
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:27,740
I forgot the rapid-fire setting was on.

338
00:21:29,020 --> 00:21:30,840
Ginbei, he's getting away!

339
00:21:38,080 --> 00:21:39,680
What a persistent bunch.

340
00:21:39,680 --> 00:21:43,240
So that means this guy
must be worth quite a lot.

341
00:21:44,320 --> 00:21:46,100
Hey! Give back the safe!

342
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:46,880
Don't come near me!

343
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:48,800
Stop!

344
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:53,680
Stop!

345
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:58,660
I said stop, you...

346
00:22:02,880 --> 00:22:30,740
Yeeeeeeeeeeeeah...
yeah, good, good, good, good, good...

347
00:22:30,740 --> 00:22:57,420
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

348
00:22:57,420 --> 00:22:59,600
We'd better check inside just in case.

349
00:23:09,060 --> 00:23:11,860
W-w-w-what is this!

350
00:23:12,640 --> 00:23:14,851
This game software is,

351
00:23:14,901 --> 00:23:17,540
a rare treasure you can't
get anymore these days.

352
00:23:17,540 --> 00:23:20,200
Thanks a lot, Kazuo.

353
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:27,100
How is this a keepsake of you and Grandma?!

354
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:33,620
T-this is the game software I used
to play with Grandma when I was a kid!

355
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:36,300
Such a thing existed 100 years ago!

356
00:23:38,020 --> 00:23:39,900
You lying, goddamn old geezer!

357
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:40,820
Gah!

358
00:23:40,860 --> 00:23:41,620
Waaaaah!

359
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:45,260
Hohoho!

360
00:23:49,220 --> 00:23:53,240
Damn it! How dare you trick me,
you goddamn old geezer!

361
00:23:53,880 --> 00:23:56,680
I'm never coming back here again, damn it!

362
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:06,140
Alright! Everyone, listen up!

363
00:24:06,420 --> 00:24:09,231
As the stand-in for the auntie
who went on a hot spring trip,

364
00:24:09,281 --> 00:24:12,000
from today, I, Kankichi Ryotsu, will
handle the plumbing, laundry, and so on.

365
00:24:13,360 --> 00:24:17,220
Don't defy what I say,
and follow it properly! Got it?

366
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:21,340
Next time, the bachelor dorm welcomes two more!
Nice to meet you!

367
00:24:43,340 --> 00:24:59,000
I want to ride a motorbike across the vast desert,
I want to be freer than a bird.

368
00:24:59,980 --> 00:25:07,140
A lady's dreams change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

369
00:25:08,920 --> 00:25:15,100
Sorry, my heart of love, I surrender.

370
00:25:15,100 --> 00:25:22,220
Panoramic future,
the dazzle comes soon enough.

371
00:25:22,220 --> 00:25:26,520
You'll understand after this, right?

372
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:30,080
Sorry, wait for me.

